body:
Actually read and instruction fetch are distinguished on many conventional busses. This subject came up in my review of the IOPMP spec recently and the maintainers there agreed that distinguishing R and X makes sense;
https://lists.riscv.org/g/tech-iopmp/message/455
I don't know why you think instruction fetches aren't conveyed over the bus? E.g. on AXI, the AxPROT[2] signal is used to distinguish a data access from an instruction access.
